    ],
    "long_instructions": "##PROTOTYPE – SC2 AI in Your Program · Who Am AI? project\r\n###This version: Starter with image generation\r\n\r\nSame code as the default starter (104027). The only difference: the **Images tab is on**, so students can make their own mystery character with the image generator. Making a character is optional and not scored.\r\n\r\n- `start_game` is locked and collapsed and holds the game rules. Keeping the secret is the student's job in `my_prompt`.\r\n\r\n**All versions**\r\n- Starter, no image generation: [104027](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/104027)\r\n- Starter with image generation (this level): [105336](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105336)\r\n- Finished sample (strong): [105337](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105337)\r\n- Calibration sample, middle: [105339](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105339)\r\n- Calibration sample, weak: [105340](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105340)\r\n- Prompt Helper (AI Chat level): [105338](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105338)\r\n\r\n**Open questions**\r\n- Is image generation funded at launch? If not, this version is cut.\r\n- Does making a character pull time away from the AI decisions the project assesses?\r\n- Should the Images tab let students make only a Character, not backgrounds or objects?"
  },
